They're two separate things (though they behave identically for this
particular purpose). From a post of mine a while back in a level-design
thread:

  There are three types of water terrain: moat (}), pool (P), and
  water (W), all of which show up on screen as '}'. Some of the
  more significant differences:

  Moat:
    cannot be dried up by fire
    can be frozen
    1/30 chance of kelp

  Pool:
    can be dried up by fire
    can be frozen
    less likely to flow into adjacent pits than a moat
    1/10 chance of kelp

  Water:
    cannot be dried up by fire
    cannot be frozen
    no chance of kelp

Any of these can come in any size.

